This morning I had a priest that was a likely winner, but he was
an extremely unlucky schmuck and died a hard death.  He was
exploring the medusa level without wearing a blindfold and was
teleporting out of control.  Unluckily, he teleported right next
to the Medusa and looked upon her before he had a chance to move
away or put on his blindfold.  How remote is the chance of this
happening?

Nevertheless, it strikes me as being instantaneous death that I
could do little about.  Of course I could have explored the level
wearing my blindfold, but this would be {boring, stupid, tedious,
time-consuming}.  And what if I didn't have a blindfold to do this
with?

It seems that you should have a chance to do something about finding
yourself next to the Medusa.  If you walk up to her without being
blind don't you have the opportunity to ID her with the / command
and then run?  Maybe I should've had this chance also.


